\f1\i0 , a factory. In Balzers. We acquired it last year as part of a money laundering\'97that is to say, diversification strategy. It produces traditional Liechtenstein Bergk\'e4se. Quite renowned locally.\'91\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise drummed her fingers on her desk. Against her better judgment, she found her lips twitching. \'91And you believe the candidate\'97who, despite his many faults, is not a complete idiot\'85\'92 She died a little inside at uttering those words and could not continue the argument.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The candidate is, forgive me, somewhat self-absorbed. If we surround him with sufficient administrative bureaucracy, creative accounting, and a few impressive-looking but ultimately meaningless demonstrations, we might buy the time you need.\'91\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise considered this. \'91How quickly can you set up a convincing executive office?\'92 She knew the trappings of the assignment would have to be first rate if they were to pull this off.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91With sufficient funding? Twenty-four hours.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91And the staff?\'91\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I can have twelve people with impressively vague job titles and the ability to generate endless paperwork by tomorrow afternoon.\'91\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What about these quantum reality lenses Alexander is expecting?\'91\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Heinrich paused. \'91There's a failing virtual reality startup in Zurich we\'92ve had our eye on. Their prototype headsets malfunction in quite interesting ways\'97users report seeing impossible colours and occasionally their own backsides without turning around. If we rebrand those as early-stage quantum imaging devices\'85\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The candidate\'92s understanding of physics begins and ends with which angle makes his cheekbones look most dramatic on camera,\'92 Eloise conceded.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91There is one small problem,\'91 Heinrich said carefully, having typed some commands into his tablet. \'91The candidate is currently on a direct flight to Zurich, which would bring him to Liechtenstein in approximately ten hours. We need more time.\'91\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise tapped a lacquered nail against her desk. \'91I can arrange some... flight plan alterations. Perhaps a sudden diversion to Rome for \'93mechanical issues\'94?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91That would be most helpful.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Consider it done.\'92 Eloise pulled up another screen on her desk and began typing. \'91Now, about this cheese factory. Is it anywhere near a dairy farm?\'92 Not that she expected Alexander to two to the difference.\
