\f1\i0 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Couldn\'92t we just park a few cows outside? Or relocate?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The factory has several advantages,\'91 Heinrich replied, warming to his theme. \'91Isolated location, high security due to proprietary recipes, large refrigerated storage areas that could easily be repurposed as \'93specialised testing chambers\'94,  and most importantly\'97it's actually functional.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91How much cheese does it produce?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Several tons monthly.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91And what do you propose we do with all this cheese while pretending it's a weapons research  lab?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We could say it's the biological medium for our experiments. Cheese cultures, bacterial growth, molecular gastronomy as a front for molecular weaponry. 
\f2\i Datentr\'e4ger-K\'e4se
\f1\i0 \'97'data carrier cheese.' Storage medium of the future.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise massaged her temple. \'91Sometimes I wonder if I'm paying you too much or not nearly enough, Heinrich.\'91\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The market rate for absurdist corporate espionage has always been difficult to establish, Frau Shakti.\'91\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Fine. Activate your cheese-based cover operation. But I want daily reports, and if the candidate starts asking too many questions, be prepared to implement the Nightshade Protocol.\'91\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Is that the memory-altering champagne or the convenient temporary kidnapping?\'91\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Let's start with the champagne. Save the kidnapping for an emergency.\'91 Eloise glanced at her watch. \'91You have twenty-four hours, Heinrich. Make it convincing.\'91\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We'll do our best.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Just get the cheese factory ready, Heinrich. And do try to find someone who can explain quantum physics convincingly while knowing absolutely nothing about it.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Ah, for that I already have the perfect candidate. My brother-in-law. He's been explaining things he doesn't understand at family dinners for twenty years.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Excellent.\'91 Eloise ended the call and swivelled in her chair to gaze out at the fluffy view of the Layer. Even by Shakti family standards, this was getting strange.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>She pulled up the flight tracker on her screen and made a few quick adjustments to Alexander's journey, ensuring at least a 36-hour delay through an improbable combination of mechanical issues, weather patterns, and a sudden, unexpected ostrich migration across an airport runway. While expensive, it was the most amusing thing she\'92d ordered all day.
